==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|maddoc|lang=enm}}, from an unrecorded {{etyl|ang}} form corresponding to Old Norse {{term|maðkr|lang=non}} (whence dialectal English {{term|mawk|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|madike|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|mask|lang=sv}}), originally a diminutive of the {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|maþô||worm|lang=gem-pro}} (whence Old English {{term|maþa|lang=ang}}), equivalent to {{suffix|made|t1=maggot|ock}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmadək/}}

